# UI juice standards (hybrid visual law)

**Doctrine:** Bible §19 and Law 10. Mode contract: `quiet-event-modes.mdc` (Bible §19.1–19.2, §19.4). Research ≠ product law.

Before any `CreateFrame` / theater / juice work: read Bible §19 and `quiet-event-modes.mdc`. Do not treat archived pre-reformation UI briefs as law.

## Hybrid visual law

- **Functional** (Director Console desks, lists, settings): stock Blizzard templates, pragmatic, opaque high-contrast, `GameFont*`. Working tools stay working tools.
- **Theatrical** (proclamations, fighter cards, seals, verdicts, Records Book, Decree): full ecclesiastical identity — dark iron, charcoal, aged parchment, muted gold; gothic/ecclesiastical typography; Warcraft-compatible ornamentation; official seals. **Non-negotiable.**
- The contrast between the plain desk and the dignified theater is the comedy engine. **The UI itself never tells jokes.** No meme clutter. The software never narrates (Law 4).
- Custom media is permitted and expected **only where theater lives**. Missing media must not fail load — fall back to default UI.
- Dual-encode status (color + text). Class color on **names** only.
- UI displays Core / Pope-ratified outcomes; never awards points, standing, or ranks (Law 1).

## Mode (juice)

- **Quiet Mode:** no toasts, no sound, no pips, no ambient surfaces. At most minimap presence and the active Decree. The **only** Quiet notice is the Bible’s gentle version-mismatch drop (§13.4 / §20.3) — see `quiet-event-modes.mdc`. Not a toast-kind family.
- **Event Mode:** consequence beats and §19.4 ceremonial cues only. Rhythm: Quiet → Ritual Begins → Spectacle → Consequence → Quiet.
- Sound is sparse and meaningful: Sanction bell, Verdict, Elevation, Knighting, Cowardice Recorded; later, Canonization seal. Quiet Mode is silent, absolutely. No ambient audio, UI clicks-and-whooshes, or notification sounds.

## Motion / timing

- Prefer show/hide + short alpha on Beef-owned **insecure** frames
- **No permanent `OnUpdate`** for juice — disable scripts when idle (`wow-performance.mdc`)
- **No center-screen** alert frames / WA-style pulses. The Fight HUD is **not** an alert pulse: Event Mode only, top-center default, movable (§10.7, §19.2). Do not ban it as “center-screen.”
- Never hitch combat
- Guest on player `uiScale` — never set `uiScale` / `UIParent:SetScale`

## Anti-patterns (reject)

WA center pulses · permanent animation directors · juice OS / tween bus · hex palette token systems · Details!-dense working desks · item-quality rainbow for ranks · glass/low-alpha panels · SecureActionButton for panels · tip jars · Retail templates unverified on Anniversary · custom media on functional surfaces · ambient SFX / UI whooshes · meme clutter · jokes in chrome copy

## Critique (before done)

1. Is this surface functional (stock) or theatrical (ecclesiastical) — and did we apply the matching law?
2. Does Quiet Mode stay silent (no toast, sound, or pip) aside from the single §13.4 version-mismatch notice?
3. Does the UI itself tell a joke or add meme clutter?
4. If custom theater media is missing, does the addon still load?

Harness ≠ spectacle — claim **POLISH:CANDIDATE** only; human signs PASS. See `verification.mdc`.
